[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5379047138","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5379047138","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5379047138,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQJ2-4g","user":{"login":"maityyy","id":47220489,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIwNDg5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47220489?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy","html_url":"https://github.com/maityyy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maityyy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-22T07:37:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-22T07:37:36Z","body":"It's actually unbelievable that the previous code worked that way, since this is a typical has/get pattern issue with hash maps. I'm wondering if there are other cases like this (there must be), or if they can't be fixed right now because `GDType` hasn't been fully implemented?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5379047138/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5390895893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5390895893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5390895893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQVKLFQ","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T04:53:03Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T04:59:18Z","body":"In preparation for the [imminent removal of method maps from `GDType`](122751), I've updated the PR to use the property map instead.\r\n\r\nWhile the property map doesn't store method pointers, our function only cares to know if it exists.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5390895893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5397249036","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5397249036","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5397249036,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQbN8DA","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T15:12:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T15:12:09Z","body":"I trust you are familiar with our [optimization pull request requirements](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/optimization.html#pull-request-requirements).\r\n\r\nI'd also ask that you give a brief explanation of what the code does and when it runs, so that I have a starting point to review the change.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5397249036/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5401156159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5401156159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5401156159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQe8aPw","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T20:44:42Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T21:18:31Z","body":"## The explanation\r\n\r\n`_profile_count_as_native()` is called to inform a non-GDScript function should be profiled, in the following situation:\r\n- The project is running inside the editor\r\n- Profiler Autostart must be enabled\r\n- The `debugger/profile_native_calls` editor setting must be enabled\r\n\r\n## GDScript test\r\nGiven the above, I did the following test.\r\n\r\nBuild command: `scons target=editor production=yes`\r\nScript:\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node\r\n\r\nconst N = 2_000_000\r\n\r\nstatic var lambdas: Array[Callable] = [\r\n\tfunc (n):\r\n\t\treturn n.is_class(\"Object\"),\r\n\tfunc (n):\r\n\t\treturn n.is_class(\"Node\"),\r\n]\r\n\r\nfunc _enter_tree():\r\n\tvar n := Node.new()\r\n\tvar s := 0\r\n\r\n\tvar t0 := Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\tfor i in N:\r\n\t\ts += int(lambdas.pick_random().call(n))\r\n\tvar t1 := Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\r\n\tvar ns_per_op := (t1 - t0) * 1000.0 / N\r\n\tprint(\"Benchmark result: %.1f ns/op, %d\" % [ns_per_op, s])\r\n\tawait get_tree().create_timer(1.0).timeout\r\n\tget_tree().quit()\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot sure if there is an oversight, but without the random lambda, `_profile_count_as_native()` only got called once per run instead of `N` times (I used a `printf` to be sure).\r\n\r\nAverage ns/op:\r\n|Build|ns/op|\r\n|-|-|\r\n|`master`|392.58|\r\n|PR|366.84|\r\n\r\n## Raw C++ Testing\r\n\r\nBuild command: `scons target=editor linker=mold dev_build=yes tests=yes`\r\nUsing the following `test_user_bench.cpp`:\r\n```cpp\r\n#include \"tests/test_macros.h\"\r\n\r\n#include \"modules/gdscript/gdscript_vm.cpp\"\r\n\r\nTEST_FORCE_LINK(test_user_bench)\r\n\r\n#include <chrono>\r\n#include <cstdio>\r\n\r\nstatic void user_bench() {\r\n\tconst int N = 5'000'000;\r\n\tstatic uintptr_t sink = 0;\r\n\r\n\tauto *n = memnew(Object());\r\n\r\n\tprintf(\"Existing function!\\n\");\r\n\tauto t0 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\r\n\t\tsink += (uintptr_t)_profile_count_as_native(n, SNAME(\"is_class\"));\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto t1 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();\r\n\r\n\tdouble ns_per_op_1 = std::chrono::duration<double, std::nano>(t1 - t0).count() / N;\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmark result: %.1f ns/op (sink %zu)\\n\", ns_per_op_1, (size_t)sink);\r\n\r\n\tprintf(\"Non-existent function!\\n\");\r\n\tauto t2 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\r\n\t\tsink += (uintptr_t)_profile_count_as_native(n, SNAME(\"i_dont_exist\"));\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto t3 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();\r\n\tdouble ns_per_op_2 = std::chrono::duration<double, std::nano>(t3 - t2).count() / N;\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmark result: %.1f ns/op (sink %zu)\\n\", ns_per_op_2, (size_t)sink);\r\n\r\n\tmemdelete(n);\r\n}\r\n\r\nREGISTER_TEST_COMMAND(\"user-bench\", &user_bench)\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Results\r\n\r\n|Build|Existing|Non-existent|\r\n|-|-|-|\r\n|`master`|90.7 ns/op|85 ns/op|\r\n|PR|27.9 ns/op|27.5 ns/op|","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5401156159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5401555231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5401555231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5401555231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQfUxHw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T21:23:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T21:23:36Z","body":"This isn't really a representative test though, the C++ benchmark doesn't really test anything useful in isolation, and the GDScript case doesn't really show significant optimization, 20 ns is not significant when it comes to GDScript\r\n\r\nHow are you accounting for cache temperature and other compounding factors in your benchmarking and evaluation of the results?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5401555231/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5401966712","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5401966712","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5401966712,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQft4eA","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T22:01:22Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T22:42:50Z","body":"In addition to the tests above, I've run a C++ profiler over the same GDScript case above.\r\n\r\nBuild command: `scons target=editor linker=mold dev_build=yes tests=yes`\r\n\r\n## Before\r\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1022\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/160cae0f-dbc1-4fe7-9049-877751b2c21e\" />\r\n\r\n## After\r\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"987\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d52da09-c668-4702-aea8-65c0b2ce23f5\" />\r\n\r\n> 20 ns is not significant when it comes to GDScript\r\n\r\nNote the optimization is aimed at the profiler (or rather, checking if a function call should be profiled), which is inevitably slow by default. I just made it a little less slow.\r\n\r\nFor reference, the same test with the profiler off is around 188 ns/op both before and after.\r\n\r\nBut I assume this case is considered too situational to be optimized? I still wouldn't agree with a profiler function calling three look-ups (one currently with no purpose other than adding weight for no reason) when it could be calling just one.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5401966712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5407583857","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5407583857","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5407583857,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQlEucQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T08:27:03Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T08:27:03Z","body":"It looks very marginal in the greater scheme of things ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5407583857/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5410765652","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5410765652","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5410765652,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQoG7VA","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T13:02:43Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T13:02:43Z","body":"Let's put this specific PR aside for a second. This is not the first time I link you to the optimization guidelines and I don't feel you have understood or acknowledged the issue, so let me spell it out for you:\r\n\r\n> Explain why you chose to optimize this code (e.g. include the profiling result, link the issue report, etc.).\r\n\r\nProfiling that you have done after the change does not satisfy this. I have the impression you are searching for anti-patterns in code and do your profiling / benchmarking after applying changes based on that. This then leads to very specific benchmarks or cases were you are measuring fluctuations but take it as confirmation for a change that looks sensible in code. \r\n\r\nThis is not an approach for optimization that we invite. We do have [documentation](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/optimization.html#choosing-what-to-optimize) on how we expect people to select what they are optimizing. You clearly have the tools at hand, so for the future I'd ask you to take a step back from code and start out with a real world use-case and profiling.\r\n\r\nGetting rid of some patterns in code might make sense, but it is a code-style question not a performance question. If that is what you are trying to do, you need to make it clear in your PR. Please be aware that for code-style, area maintainers might have different requirements and priorities. For GDScript in particular I am not interested in doing cleanup of common anti-patterns on a function granularity. I'm also not interested in introducing `GDType` in cold code at this point, the maintenance burden resulting from the regular changes to the system is not worth it. In general please reach out to the relevant people on RC before trying to do style adjustments, to see if there is interest in it.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn regard to this specific change. The code is relevant to profiling of dynamic code (call opcodes which could not be validated at compile time). This does not seem relevant enough to introduce GDType to me. However the `ClassDB::class_exists(cname)` check actually does not make any sense given that `cname` is directly obtained from `Object::get_class_name`. If you want to reduce this PR to getting RID of that check, I'd be on board with it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5410765652/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5410923572","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5410923572","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5410923572,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQoQkNA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T13:15:46Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T13:17:09Z","body":"Also, for the future, please always list detailed system information on your benchmarks, especially the CPU specs and memory details (I'll make a PR clarifying this in the optimization guidelines soon)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5410923572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5413305640","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5413305640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5413305640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQqh9KA","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T16:13:21Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T16:13:45Z","body":"> In regard to this specific change. The code is relevant to profiling of dynamic code (call opcodes which could not be validated at compile time). This does not seem relevant enough to introduce GDType to me. However the `ClassDB::class_exists(cname)` check actually does not make any sense given that `cname` is directly obtained from `Object::get_class_name`. If you want to reduce this PR to getting RID of that check, I'd be on board with it.\r\n\r\nDone.\r\n\r\nAs for introducing `GDType` in GDScript, I have agreed it's best to wait until it's complete. In a near future, it should be possible to make the VM independent of `ClassDB`, but that's not the time yet.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5413305640/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5511370120","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122706#issuecomment-5511370120","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122706","id":5511370120,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSIDViA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/use